# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NO PROVIDER API KEY BELONGS IN THIS FILE.
#
# The frontend never holds a provider key or LiteLLM virtual key. It sends a
# Firebase ID token to same-origin Vercel APIs; those APIs derive a capped
# per-user virtual key and call LiteLLM server-to-server. Provider keys
# (DeepSeek, Gemini, OpenAI) live only on Railway.
#
# Anything prefixed VITE_ is inlined into the browser bundle at build time.
# A real key in a VITE_ variable is published to every visitor, permanently,
# in a file anyone can read. There is no such variable any more — do not add
# one back.
#
# Server-side only (set in the Vercel dashboard, never in this file):
#   LITELLM_MASTER_KEY
#   LITELLM_KEY_DERIVATION_SECRET (independent from LITELLM_MASTER_KEY)
#   LITELLM_GATEWAY_URL (explicit per Vercel environment)
#   FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON (or split Firebase Admin values)
#   UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL / UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN (required on Vercel)
#   CIRQLE_AI_NEW_KEYS_PER_DAY (optional global issuance circuit breaker;
#     defaults to 25 new managed AI keys per rolling day)
#   FIREBASE_APP_CHECK_ENFORCED (after monitor-mode validation only)
#   CRON_SECRET (random 32+ character bearer secret for daily maintenance)
#   INTEGRATIONS_LIVE_ENABLED=true (explicit Google live-mode gate)
#   INTEGRATIONS_APP_ORIGIN (exact canonical HTTPS Vercel origin)
#   GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID / GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET (server-side OAuth client)
#   GOOGLE_TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY (base64-encoded 32-byte AES key; keep stable
#     across deploys and rotate only with a credential-migration plan)
#   GOOGLE_OAUTH_TEST_MODE=true (only while the Google app is in Testing)
#   FIREBASE_WEB_API_KEY (optional smoke-test override; the checked-in public
#     Firebase app config is used when this is absent)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.
# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.
# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.
APP_URL="MY_APP_URL"

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Everything below is OPTIONAL. Leave it all unset and the app runs in
# preview mode: Calendar, Gmail and digest email use realistic sample data,
# every screen is fully interactive, and each one wears a "Preview" label so
# a demo can't be mistaken for a live connection.
#
# Step-by-step instructions for going live: MANUAL_SETUP.md at the repo root.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# reCAPTCHA Enterprise site key registered for Firebase App Check. This is a
# public site key, not a secret. Omit it for local development.
# VITE_FIREBASE_APP_CHECK_SITE_KEY="6L..."

# Required for every Vercel Preview deployment. Supply the one-line web-app
# config JSON for the isolated staging Firebase project. Preview builds fail
# closed if this is absent or points at production; production builds refuse
# an override that points away from cirqle-9dd06.
# VITE_FIREBASE_CONFIG_JSON='{"apiKey":"...","authDomain":"cirqle-staging.firebaseapp.com","projectId":"cirqle-staging","appId":"...","firestoreDatabaseId":"(default)"}'

# The production Dashboard hides sample-data seeding. Enable only in a
# disposable demo deployment whose data cannot be confused with a real CRM.
# VITE_ENABLE_DEMO_DATA="true"

# Optional local-only escape hatch when running Vite without Vercel functions
# or while intentionally offline. Local strength/common-password checks remain
# enforced, but the Pwned Passwords k-anonymity lookup is skipped. Never set
# this in a production or shared preview deployment.
# VITE_PASSWORD_BREACH_CHECK_DISABLED="true"

# Vercel sends this server-only bearer secret to the daily, bounded retention
# and contact-maintenance job. Generate a unique random value of at least
# 32 characters in the Vercel dashboard; never prefix it with VITE_.
# CRON_SECRET="set-only-in-vercel"

# Local Firebase emulator (auth :9099, firestore :8085). Development only.
# VITE_USE_FIREBASE_EMULATOR=true

# Google Calendar + Gmail browser gate. BOTH values are required. The API base
# must be a same-origin path; external origins are rejected. Client id, client
# secret, OAuth state and refresh tokens remain server-only.
# VITE_INTEGRATIONS_MODE=live
# Base path of the Vercel APIs that mediate token exchange and all
# Google API calls. The browser never holds a refresh token.
# VITE_INTEGRATIONS_API_BASE="/api/integrations"

# Transactional email for the dormant-contact digest. The in-app digest
# works without this; only emailing it out needs a provider.
# VITE_EMAIL_MODE=live
# VITE_EMAIL_FROM="you@yourdomain.com"

# Disposable production-candidate smoke test. Use a Vercel preview URL. The
# script refuses the production hostname unless CIRQLE_SMOKE_ALLOW_PRODUCTION
# is deliberately set to true. It creates one verified email/password user,
# makes one tiny fast-tier call, deletes every account layer, and prints no
# credentials.
# CIRQLE_SMOKE_BASE_URL="https://cirqle-git-hardening-example.vercel.app"
# CIRQLE_SMOKE_CONFIRM="create-and-delete-disposable-cirqle-user"
# CIRQLE_SMOKE_ALLOW_PRODUCTION="false"
